+{"action_plan":"P0 (1-5 days):\nP0-A Security: (1) sanitize thread_id in threadFilePath for ALL readers/writers + regression test ../config; (2) mcp.add/update stdio requires L2 or arm phrase + optional LOLBIN denylist, do not silent-enable mcp; (3) redact mcp.list/servers_updated env/headers; scrub stdio env to PATH+explicit config.env only.\nP0-B Lifecycle/multi-peer: (4) supersede uses same abortThreadChatFull as chat.abort + generation-token CAS in finally; (5) stamp pendingToolCalls.originWs and scope applyConnectionCloseGracePeriod per socket; (6) wire AbortSignal + tool.cancel to extension path; stamp thread_id in dispatchToExtension (analyze_image).\nP0-C Persistence: (7) redact tool rows before threadManager.addMessage (mirror history redactForStorage).\nP0-D Computer-use macOS: (8) fix cuPidForWindow via cuWindowInfoDict fail-closed; (9) implement occlusion/onscreen or stop advertising flags; fail-closed FOREGROUND_RAISE_FAILED for injective actions.\nP0-E Ops: (10) tray launchd template must match install-daemon.sh (daemon start --daemonize + KeepAlive).\nP0-F Spike: (11) hud.spike.confirm_response → respondFrom(ws) or isolate spike confirmation IDs.\n\nP1 (1-2 weeks):\n(12) always pass {originWs:ws} for all L2_GATE_TOOLS + dual-peer origin_mismatch tests; (13) session-trust never auto-approves danger/experimental/task_induced_dialog; (14) history redact shell.command/host_write.body/mcp meta-tools; (15) corrupt index/thread fail-closed with backup (invert silent-empty tests); (16) executeMcpTool hard-gate manual active_mcp_server_ids; fix DESTRUCTIVE snake_case; scan schema titles/examples; SIGTERM→SIGKILL MCP children; (17) graceful shutdown drains CU/LLM/pending/leases/confirmations; (18) release needs CI tests+audit; hard-require host/tray; SBOM+SHA256SUMS; (19) supersede ADR-006; refresh architecture protocol inventory; (20) skill craft yaml.dump+type allowlist+confirm; sanitize use_skill.\n\nP2 debt:\n(21) split server.ts into auth/admission/tools/protocol/lifecycle; (22) shared packages/ws-protocol + default-deny validateWsMessage; (23) protocol_version hello + single VERSION; (24) token/cost budget + full publicsuffix; (25) boot real startServer in tests; platform-independent CU gates on Linux CI; regression tests for every High; (26) Developer ID/notarize/Authenticode; (27) streaming store slices + computer-task-mirror chrome.storage persistence.","confirmed_critical":0,"confirmed_detail":[{"finding":{"category":"abort/cancel","confidence":"confirmed","evidence":"On new chat.create, only `existing.abort()` is called. Unlike chat.abort (message-router.ts:728-745) there is no `rejectPendingForThread`, `securityConfirmations.rejectForWorker`, or computer-task flip. Extension dispatch Promise in server.ts:2196-2314 never observes AbortSignal — only pending map rejection ends it. Mid-CDP tools run until 15s timeout; L2 dialogs can sit until confirmation timeout; concurrent new chat can race in-flight tools.","file":"companion/src/message-router.ts:433-438","fix_hint":"On supersede (and any abortThreadChat caller), also call rejectPendingForThread(threadId), securityConfirmations.rejectForWorker(threadId), flipAllComputerTaskAborts, and wire signal.abort into extension pending resolvers.","id":"LLM-1","impact":"Stop-by-resend leaves browser CDP and confirmation UI live; user believes prior run stopped while tools continue executing on real tabs.","prior_status":"new","severity":"high","title":"chat.create supersede aborts LLM only — does not drain extension tools or L2"},"verdict":{"evidence":"message-router.ts chat.create:433-438 only existing.abort(); chat.abort:728-754 does rejectForWorker + rejectPendingForThread + lease release; server.ts:5466-5473 flipAllComputerTaskAborts only on chat.abort; server.ts createToolExecutor extension Promise ~2196-2314 no AbortSignal listener (pendingToolCalls + timeout only); TOOL_EXECUTION_TIMEOUT_MS=15000; adapter passes signal to executeTool but extension path ignores it; App.tsx handleSend→chat.send→chat.create, handleStop→chat.abort.","finding_id":"LLM-1","real":true,"reason":"Confirmed asymmetry: chat.create supersede only calls existing.abort() on the thread AbortController; unlike chat.abort it never rejectPendingForThread, rejectForWorker, releaseLeases, or flipAllComputerTaskAborts. Extension tool.execute Promise does not observe AbortSignal (only pending map rejection/timeout ends it); MCP alone honors signal. UI resend uses chat.create without prior chat.abort, so mid-CDP tools, L2 dialogs (45s), and host_computer can continue while a new run starts. Explicit Stop (chat.abort) does full drain—so impact is supersede/resend residual, not broken Stop—hence medium not high.","severity_adjusted":"medium"}},{"finding":{"category":"data-exposure","confidence":"confirmed","evidence":"createToolResultMessage stores `content: JSON.stringify(result)` and `tool_calls: [{ params, result }]` with no redaction. adapter.ts:807 `threadManager.addMessage(...)` writes that to ~/.cmspark-agent/threads. history/store.ts:83-126 redacts cookies/evaluate/MCP/shell for history.db only — threads are the durable conversation used by rebuildMessagesFromHistory.","file":"companion/src/llm/adapter.ts:119-130","fix_hint":"Apply the same redactForStorage policy (or stronger) before addMessage for tool rows; keep full results only ephemerally for the current LLM round if needed.","id":"LLM-2","impact":"Cookie values, evaluate outputs, shell stdout, MCP file reads, and secrets remain on disk in thread JSON; export/backup/filesystem access can exfiltrate session material that history.db intentionally strips.","prior_status":"partial","severity":"high","title":"Thread message store persists full unredacted tool params and results"},"verdict":{"evidence":"adapter.ts:119-130 createToolResultMessage sets content: JSON.stringify(result) and tool_calls:[{params, result}] with no redaction; adapter.ts:807 threadManager.addMessage(threadId, createToolResultMessage(...)); adapter.ts:203-211 rebuildMessagesFromHistory uses JSON.stringify(tc.result). history/store.ts:22-35 SENSITIVE_COOKIE_TOOLS/SENSITIVE_CODE_TOOLS + shell_exec; store.ts:442-448 redactForStorage only on history.db record(). thread-manager.ts:503-530 addMessage pushes raw message then atomicWriteJSON (io.ts:16 default 0o600). markdown-export.ts renderToolEntry only length-bounds JSON (MAX_RESULT_JSON_LEN=2000), no secret redaction.","finding_id":"LLM-2","real":true,"reason":"Confirmed: createToolResultMessage + threadManager.addMessage persist full unredacted tool params/results to ~/.cmspark-agent/threads/*.json; rebuildMessagesFromHistory consumes tc.result from that store. history/store.ts redactForStorage redacts cookies/code/MCP/shell for history.db only — intentional asymmetry. Mitigations (0o600 atomicWriteJSON, functional need for multi-turn LLM) reduce multi-user exposure but do not remove durable cookie/session and secret material from thread JSON or length-bounded exports. Impact for get_cookies and sensitive MCP reads matches the session-hijack threat history.db was fixed for.","severity_adjusted":"high"}},{"finding":{"category":"capability-gate","confidence":"confirmed","evidence":"adapter: `if (mcpSelectionMode === \"manual\") { mcpTools = mcpManager.getAggregatedToolsForServers(activeServerIds) }` — visibility only. executeMcpTool: `const route = manager.resolveToolName(toolName)` uses full `aggregated.aliases` with no thread/active_mcp_server_ids check. Manager comment admits aliases exist so router can dispatch; selection never re-checked at call time.","file":"companion/src/llm/adapter.ts:428-436; companion/src/server.ts:4025-4037; companion/src/mcp/manager.ts:287-311","fix_hint":"In executeMcpTool (and executeMcpMetaTool), load acting thread mcp_selection_mode/active_mcp_server_ids; if manual, reject when route.serverName not in active set. Mirror isToolAllowed hard-gate style.","id":"MCP-1","impact":"Thread marked manual with a subset of servers can still execute tools on any connected server if the model invents/recalls a namespaced name (or pack/tool_whitelist does not list exact mcp__ names). Undermines intended isolation between MCP servers.","prior_status":"new","severity":"high","title":"Per-thread mcp_selection_mode=manual only filters LLM tool list, not execute path"},"verdict":{"evidence":"adapter.ts:432-436: if (mcpSelectionMode === \"manual\") { mcpTools = mcpManager.getAggregatedToolsForServers(activeServerIds) } else { mcpTools = mcpManager.getAggregatedTools() }. manager.ts:297-312: getAggregatedToolsForServers only returns filtered definitions; resolveToolName uses this.aggregated.aliases.get(namespacedName) with no server allow-list. manager.ts:291-293 falsely claims dropped aliases mean \"the router can't dispatch\". server.ts:2182-2184: isMcpNamespaced → executeMcpTool with no thread selection gate. server.ts:4033-4037: route = manager.resolveToolName(toolName); only fails if not found. thread-manager.ts:554-558: isToolAllowed returns true when tool_whitelist is null (default).","finding_id":"MCP-1","real":true,"reason":"Confirmed: mcp_selection_mode=manual only filters LLM tool definitions in adapter.ts; executeMcpTool resolves via full aggregated.aliases with no thread/active_mcp_server_ids check. Manager comment claiming aliases are dropped so the router cannot dispatch is false. Impact is real for default threads (tool_whitelist=null) if the model invents/recalls mcp__ names, but lower than claimed high: pack allowlists hard-block unlisted names via isToolAllowed, and trust/capability confirms still gate many calls. Original audit item 7 was visibility-only by design.","severity_adjusted":"medium"}},{"finding":{"category":"secrets-exposure","confidence":"confirmed","evidence":"McpServerMeta.config documents: \"Sensitive values (env, headers) included\". mcp.list returns `getMcpManager().listServers()` with full config. servers_updated broadcasts metas/listServers() unredacted. By contrast redactConfigForBroadcast masks mcp.servers env/headers values to \"***\" for config.updated.","file":"companion/src/mcp/types.ts:109-112; companion/src/message-router.ts:1074-1076; companion/src/server.ts:5209-5216; companion/src/server.ts:4568-4615","fix_hint":"Reuse redactConfigForBroadcast-style masking when serializing McpServerMeta for WS; keep plaintext only for local disk/edit apply path, not outbound list/status events.","id":"MCP-2","impact":"Any authenticated WS peer (multi-panel / multi-peer) receives API keys and Authorization headers configured for MCP HTTP/stdio servers, defeating the redaction applied on config.updated.","prior_status":"new","severity":"high","title":"mcp.list / mcp.servers.updated broadcast unredacted env and headers"},"verdict":{"evidence":"types.ts:109-112 documents \"Sensitive values (env, headers) included\"; client.ts:81 config: { ...this._config }; message-router.ts:1074-1076 mcp.list → listServers(); server.ts:5209-5216 broadcastToClients({ type: \"mcp.servers.updated\", servers: metas|listServers() }) with no redact; server.ts:4568-4615 + 5292-5294 redactConfigForBroadcast masks env/headers only on config.updated. No mcp.list/servers_updated redaction tests; config-broadcast-redact.test.ts covers only config.updated path.","finding_id":"MCP-2","real":true,"reason":"Confirmed by reading current code: McpServerMeta intentionally embeds full McpServerConfig; client.getMeta() shallow-copies _config (env/headers); mcp.list and mcp.add/update/delete/toggle responses return getMcpManager().listServers() unredacted; servers_updated/tools_changed broadcast metas/listServers() via broadcastToClients with no redaction. By contrast config.updated uses redactConfigForBroadcast which masks mcp.servers env/headers values to \"***\". Mitigations: only authenticated peers receive broadcasts, WS is loopback, and UI edit form depends on plaintext—so not unauthenticated RCE-class exposure, but multi-peer still receives secrets and that defeats SRV-1-style redaction. Severity lowered from high to medium for auth+loopback boundary.","severity_adjusted":"medium"}},{"finding":{"category":"inject-safety / TOCTOU","confidence":"confirmed","evidence":"cuInject accepts checkOcclusion/checkOnscreen but only uses checkSecureInput and estopFlag — never branches on checkOcclusion. Adapter still passes \"--check-occlusion\". postEventDual clears process pin and event.post(.cghidEventTap) so HID delivers to frontmost window under cursor after activate.","file":"companion/src/host-use/darwin/host.swift:1689-1711,1675-1686; companion/src/computer/darwin-adapters.ts:715-718","fix_hint":"Implement occlusion (window-at-point / layer ownership == target windowId) and onscreen checks when flags true; fail with CLICK_OCCLUDED. Prefer SkyLight-only when trusted, or require FG raise success before HID. Add unit/integration tests that assert flag rejects covered coordinates.","id":"COMP-1","impact":"TS layer believes click occlusion is enforced; when Chrome/side panel or another window covers the target, inject can still report ok while the physical click lands on a non-whitelisted UI (documented b0faek/psl8ci class). Trust-root for \"I only authorized WeChat\" is weakened.","prior_status":"new","severity":"high","title":"macOS --check-occlusion / --check-onscreen are dead flags; HID dual-post can misroute clicks"},"verdict":{"evidence":"host.swift:1689-1691 cuInject only uses checkSecureInput + estopFlag; checkOcclusion/checkOnscreen never read in body (grep: only signature+argv at :687). host.swift:1675-1686 postEventDual sets eventTargetUnixProcessID=0 then event.post(.cghidEventTap); success = skyOk || useHid. darwin-adapters.ts:715-718 click always passes --check-occlusion; :743-746 type passes --check-onscreen; :702-708 preferForeground swallows non-probe raise failures. host.swift:1040 comment claims '--check-occlusion on inject' handles occlusion; :1706 host still _ = cuActivatePid(pid). Contrast Windows computer-input.ps1:321-331 Assert-Landing WindowFromPoint OCCLUDED fail-closed. host-skylight.swift:1104-1106 same dead params.","finding_id":"COMP-1","real":true,"reason":"Independently confirmed: cuInject accepts checkOcclusion/checkOnscreen but only gates on checkSecureInput and estopFlag; darwin-adapters still pass --check-occlusion/--check-onscreen; comments falsely claim occlusion defense-in-depth. postEventDual clears PID pin and HID-posts, so residual overlay/FG-race misroute is real—especially with preferForeground swallowing FOREGROUND_RAISE_FAILED and host ignoring cuActivatePid result. Not high: SkyLight remains PID-pinned, host activates before inject by default, and computer-use L2/whitelist still gate tool invocation; Windows has real WindowFromPoint OCCLUDED, Darwin does not. Impact is false safety contract + residual misroute, not unconstrained off-whitelist inject.","severity_adjusted":"medium"}},{"finding":{"category":"inject-safety / correctness","confidence":"confirmed","evidence":"func cuPidForWindow: CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo([.optionAll], windowId) then windows.first for PID. Sibling cuWindowInfoDict correctly searches by kCGWindowNumber; inject/activate paths call cuPidForWindow instead.","file":"companion/src/host-use/darwin/host.swift:797-801","fix_hint":"Resolve PID via cuWindowInfoDict(windowId:)[kCGWindowOwnerPID]; fail closed if missing. Share one resolver with screenshot/AX paths.","id":"COMP-2","impact":"SkyLight pin and cuActivatePid may target the wrong process (often frontmost/z-order head). Compounds COMP-1 HID misroute and FOREGROUND races after side-panel Allow.","prior_status":"new","severity":"high","title":"cuPidForWindow ignores windowId — uses first CGWindowList entry under optionAll"},"verdict":{"evidence":"host.swift:797-801:\nfunc cuPidForWindow(_ windowId: UInt32) -> pid_t {\n    guard let windows = CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo([.optionAll], windowId) as? [[String: Any]],\n          let first = windows.first,\n          let pid = first[kCGWindowOwnerPID as String] as? pid_t else { return 0 }\n    return pid\n}\n\nContrast cuWindowInfoDict (779-794) which uses first(where: { cuWindowNumber($0) == windowId }) on IncludingWindow / OnScreenOnly / optionAll.\n\ncuInject (1692-1706): let pid = cuPidForWindow(windowId); _ = cuActivatePid(pid); then postEventDual pins eventTargetUnixProcessID to that pid.\nSame bug at host-skylight.swift:646-650.","finding_id":"COMP-2","real":true,"reason":"cuPidForWindow calls CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo([.optionAll], windowId) and returns windows.first's kCGWindowOwnerPID without matching kCGWindowNumber. With optionAll, relativeToWindow does not filter; first entry is front-to-back head (usually frontmost). Sibling cuWindowInfoDict correctly filters by id and comments ban unfiltered optionAll. inject/activate/AX/screenshot paths all use the broken helper (duplicated in host-skylight.swift). After Side Panel Allow, frontmost is often Chrome, so SkyLight pin and cuActivatePid can target the wrong process. No tests or flags mitigate this.","severity_adjusted":"high"}},{"finding":{"category":"FOREGROUND-YIELD / fail-open","confidence":"confirmed","evidence":"ensureForeground throws FOREGROUND_RAISE_FAILED when raise fails; preferForeground only rethrows ForegroundProbeBrokenError and swallows raise failure. click/type/key call preferForeground then inject. Comments admit type/key lack occlusion guard.","file":"companion/src/computer/darwin-adapters.ts:664-708,710-713","fix_hint":"Fail closed on FOREGROUND_RAISE_FAILED for injective actions, or re-L2; only soft-skip when SkyLight-only delivery is verified and occlusion check passes.","id":"COMP-3","impact":"Product tradeoff for WeChat key-window reliability becomes fail-open: inject proceeds without confirmed frontmost target, amplifying mis-click/type under Chrome contention.","prior_status":"new","severity":"high","title":"preferForeground soft-fails FOREGROUND_RAISE_FAILED then still injects"},"verdict":{"evidence":"darwin-adapters.ts preferForeground: try { await this.ensureForeground(hwnd) } catch (err) { if (err instanceof ForegroundProbeBrokenError) throw err } — FOREGROUND_RAISE_FAILED not rethrown. ensureForeground on !raised: throw new ComputerError(\"FOREGROUND_RAISE_FAILED\", ...). click/typeText/keyChord: await this.preferForeground(hwnd) then inject. preferForeground comment: \"Soft-best-effort: raise failure does not block inject except hard probe-broken.\" types.ts FOREGROUND_RAISE_FAILED: \"Precondition guard failed → inject must NOT proceed.\" host.swift cuInject: _ = cuActivatePid(pid) then postEventDual (SkyLight+HID); checkOcclusion parameter never read.","finding_id":"COMP-3","real":true,"reason":"Confirmed: preferForeground catches ensureForeground errors and rethrows only ForegroundProbeBrokenError, so ComputerError(FOREGROUND_RAISE_FAILED) is swallowed and click/typeText/keyChord still inject. That contradicts types.ts ('inject must NOT proceed') and the product brief (surface FOREGROUND_RAISE_FAILED). Impact is real under Chrome contention because host inject dual-posts HID to frontmost-under-cursor after a weak cuActivatePid, while companion osascript raise is the stronger path already failed. Not full high/refuted: soft-best-effort is an explicit product comment, probe-broken still fail-closed, and host always attempts activate. Darwin --check-occlusion is a dead flag (unused in host.swift/host-skylight.swift), so click is not better-guarded than type/key.","severity_adjusted":"medium"}},{"finding":{"category":"path-traversal / integrity","confidence":"confirmed","evidence":"private threadFilePath(threadId: string): string { return path.join(getConfigDir(), \"threads\", `${threadId}.json`) } — only create() calls sanitizeId (alphanumeric/hyphen/underscore). getMessages/addMessage/updateMessage/deleteMessagesFrom/delete use raw threadId. path.join normalizes '..', so thread_id '../config' resolves to ~/.cmspark-agent/config.json; addMessage atomicWriteJSON would overwrite it with {messages:[...]}; delete would unlinkSync it. message-router passes rest.thread_id through without sanitization.","file":"companion/src/threads/thread-manager.ts:242-244","fix_hint":"Resolve path and require realpath containment under threads/; or apply sanitizeId (reject '..' / path seps) in threadFilePath for ALL readers/writers, not only create().","id":"PERS-1","impact":"Authenticated peer (or compromised extension holding ws_secret) can corrupt or delete config.json / other DATA_DIR JSON via crafted thread_id on message or delete APIs — silent data loss of API keys, domains, MCP/apps config.","prior_status":"new","severity":"high","title":"threadFilePath does not sanitize thread_id — path escape under DATA_DIR"},"verdict":{"evidence":"companion/src/threads/thread-manager.ts:242-244 threadFilePath = path.join(getConfigDir(),'threads',`${threadId}.json`) with no sanitize; 265-269 sanitizeId only used at create() line 275; delete() 312-315 filter+saveIndex then unlinkSync(threadFilePath(threadId)) even if id absent; addMessage 510-530 read-or-empty then atomicWriteJSON(filePath). message-router.ts thread.delete: threadManager.delete(rest.thread_id) no check. server.ts thread.delete validator: only typeof string. adapter chatCreate line 292 addMessage(threadId) without existence gate.","finding_id":"PERS-1","real":true,"reason":"Confirmed: threadFilePath joins unsanitized threadId; sanitizeId only in create(). delete() always unlinkSync(threadFilePath) with no index membership check; message-router thread.delete and server schema pass any non-empty string. path.join normalizes '..' so thread_id '../config' → DATA_DIR/config.json (delete or addMessage overwrite with {messages}); 'index' hits threads/index.json. Auth required (ws_secret) and config.set already exists, but this bypasses config validation and enables silent delete/corrupt of arbitrary reachable *.json — still high integrity impact.","severity_adjusted":"high"}},{"finding":{"category":"release-signing","confidence":"confirmed","evidence":"create-dmg.sh: `codesign --force --deep --sign - --options runtime` (ad-hoc identity only). release.yml body documents binaries are not Developer ID–codesigned / notarized / Authenticode-signed. build-windows-exe.ps1 only removes signatures with signtool when present — never signs. Gatekeeper/SmartScreen warn; ad-hoc reinstall churns TCC CDHash.","file":"scripts/create-dmg.sh:102-106","fix_hint":"Procure Apple Developer ID + notarytool in release.yml; Windows EV/Authenticode in package/NSIS path; keep ad-hoc only for local TCC smoke.","id":"OPS-1","impact":"Users face OS trust warnings; macOS TCC grants can reset on rebuild; Windows SmartScreen friction; cannot claim distribution-grade binary provenance.","prior_status":"partial","severity":"high","title":"No Developer ID / notarization / Authenticode on ship artifacts"},"verdict":{"evidence":"scripts/create-dmg.sh:104-106: `codesign --force --deep --sign - --options runtime` (ad-hoc). .github/workflows/release.yml:163-167: binaries are **not** Developer ID–codesigned / notarized / Authenticode-signed (pending certificates). scripts/build-windows-exe.ps1:156-165: `signtool remove /s` only when present; never `signtool sign`. No notarytool/Developer ID Application/`signtool sign` in ship pipeline.","finding_id":"OPS-1","real":true,"reason":"Confirmed: create-dmg.sh uses ad-hoc codesign only (`--sign -`); release.yml explicitly states no Developer ID/notarization/Authenticode; build-windows-exe.ps1 only removes signatures via signtool and never signs. No notarytool/signtool-sign/Developer ID path exists in CI. Impact is real (Gatekeeper/SmartScreen friction; ad-hoc reinstall can churn TCC CDHash) but is known, disclosed, partially mitigated by ad-hoc deep-sign for local TCC, and intentionally deferred (D9/P1 cert procurement)—not a runtime exploit path. Severity lowered from high to medium.","severity_adjusted":"medium"}},{"finding":{"category":"coverage_gap_auth_handshake","confidence":"confirmed","evidence":"Test comment: \"The production gate lives inside startServer()'s connection handler, which NO test calls directly\". startAuthedServer() reimplements challenge/handshake/terminate. Production: \"Keep in sync with ... ws-auth-handshake.test.ts (which replicates this exact gate, since no test calls startServer())\".","file":"companion/tests/integration/ws-auth-handshake.test.ts:7-12,178-182; companion/src/server.ts:5391-5392,5092","fix_hint":"Add one ephemeral-port integration that boots real startServer (or extract connection handler and unit/integration test the production function once), then delete the replica over time.","id":"TEST-1","impact":"A drift in startServer wiring (message order, markPaired, computer.state push, ping keepalive, pre-auth harvest) can ship while replica tests stay green — highest remaining trust-root coverage hole.","prior_status":"partial","severity":"high","title":"startServer() never called; WS auth gate is a test-side replica"},"verdict":{"evidence":"Test header (ws-auth-handshake.test.ts:7-12): \"production gate lives inside startServer()'s connection handler, which NO test calls directly\" / \"we replicate the auth gate here\". Replica startAuthedServer (L178-231) only does issueChallenge→verifyProof→auth.ok+connected; no markPaired/computer.state/size/validateWsMessage/idempotent handshake/ping. Production (server.ts:5306-5435) has full gate including markPaired() + computer.state push; comment L5391-5392 admits replica. Grep of companion/tests: zero startServer() call sites; only extracted helpers imported from server.ts. Crypto unit-tested via production imports (L28-53, L128-166); markPaired covered in ws-auth-paired-marker.test.ts.","finding_id":"TEST-1","real":true,"reason":"Confirmed: no test calls startServer(); ws-auth-handshake uses a bare-wss replica explicitly documented as out of sync risk with production connection-handler wiring (markPaired, computer.state, validateWsMessage order, ping, idempotent handshake). Not a production vulnerability: crypto and proof verify run against real ws-auth modules; pre-auth reject/wrong-proof/happy-path are covered by the replica; markPaired has separate unit tests. High is inflated for known intentional dual-maintenance coverage debt.","severity_adjusted":"medium"}},{"finding":{"category":"test_authenticity","confidence":"confirmed","evidence":"Static import createToolExecutor from server with no _*-setup; mockWs() only {readyState:1, send:noop}. Comment admits confirmation \"times out at the 45s confirmation gate\"; only assert success===false. DEFAULT_SECURITY_CONFIRMATION_TIMEOUT_MS = 45000.","file":"companion/tests/integration/evaluate-token.test.ts:3-38; companion/src/security-confirmation.ts:6","fix_hint":"Reuse security-gates harness (real WS + CMSPARK_DATA_DIR setup); assert confirmation.request emitted and deny/timeout with short timeoutMs injection; never rely on 45s default.","id":"TEST-2","impact":"On default config CI pays ~45s hang; on a developer machine whose real DATA_DIR has auto_approve_dangerous, behavior diverges. Weak assertion cannot pin strip-vs-invalid-token contract beyond \"didn't succeed\".","prior_status":"new","severity":"high","title":"evaluate-token integration uses mock WS, no DATA_DIR isolation, can block 45s"},"verdict":{"evidence":"evaluate-token.test.ts: import createToolExecutor with no _*-setup; mockWs={readyState:1,send:noop}; only assert.equal(result.success,false); comments admit 45s confirm hang. server.ts: strip LLM security_token then L2 if !security_token; readyState!==OPEN → unavailable (dead for this mock); else securityConfirmations.request. security-confirmation.ts: DEFAULT_SECURITY_CONFIRMATION_TIMEOUT_MS=45000 used by manager constructor + setTimeout. This machine ~/.cmspark-agent/config.json has auto_approve_dangerous:true and allow_all_schemes:true (path divergence). Mitigations: tests/integration/_security-gates-setup.ts + security-gates.test.ts W8 cases (host_read + evaluate replay) assert confirmation.request after strip with isolated DATA_DIR.","finding_id":"TEST-2","real":true,"reason":"The first evaluate-token integration case is genuinely weak and slow: mockWs sets readyState=1 so L2 confirmation runs and defaults to DEFAULT_SECURITY_CONFIRMATION_TIMEOUT_MS (45s); there is no CMSPARK_DATA_DIR setup (unlike security-gates), so real auto_approve_dangerous/allow_all_schemes can divert the path (e.g. 15s tool dispatch timeout) while still asserting only success===false. That assert cannot distinguish W8 strip→gate from the pre-strip Invalid-token reject for a bogus token. Severity is not high: this is test hygiene/CI tax, not a product bug, and security-gates already pins evaluate strip with isolated DATA_DIR, real WS, and confirmation.request observation. The H2 issueToken/validateToken unit case in the same file is fine.","severity_adjusted":"medium"}},{"finding":{"category":"coverage_gap_computer_use","confidence":"confirmed","evidence":"const WIN = process.platform === \"win32\"; all three R1 tests use { skip: !WIN }. CI runs-on: ubuntu-latest so npm test never executes mutex/L2 admission properties for host_computer.","file":"companion/tests/integration/computer-task-mutex.test.ts:41,196-229; .github/workflows/ci.yml:10-11,56-58","fix_hint":"Factor platform-independent gate logic for registry busy checks and run those on all OS; keep real-ps1 smoke as win32-only.","id":"TEST-3","impact":"COMPUTER_TASK_BUSY pre-dialog and check-and-set race regressions can land without CI red; only win32 developers exercise this path.","prior_status":"new","severity":"high","title":"host_computer task-mutex integration fully skipped on Linux CI"},"verdict":{"evidence":"companion/tests/integration/computer-task-mutex.test.ts:41 const WIN = process.platform === \"win32\"; lines 196,210,229: test(..., { skip: !WIN }, ...). Comment L19: \"All tests are win32-only\". .github/workflows/ci.yml:10-11 runs-on: ubuntu-latest; 56-58: cd companion && npm test. server.ts:808-810 hostComputerGated only for win32||darwin; 3757-3759 Linux returns platform error before 3771-3778 mutex check-and-set; 3892 computerEstopEnsureOverride only on Windows branch. Grep: COMPUTER_TASK_BUSY only in server.ts + computer-task-mutex.test.ts among tests.","finding_id":"TEST-3","real":true,"reason":"Independently confirmed: computer-task-mutex.test.ts defines WIN = process.platform === \"win32\" and all three R1 tests use { skip: !WIN }; CI job runs only on ubuntu-latest and runs companion npm test, so those cases never execute in CI. COMPUTER_TASK_BUSY appears in no other test. Severity reduced from high: this is a CI/platform coverage gap, not a missing production mutex (pre-dialog + handler check-and-set exist in server.ts); on Linux host_computer is gated off before the mutex path; the concurrent race test depends on Windows-only computerEstopEnsureOverride. Related abort-registry tests still run cross-platform but do not assert admission/BUSY.","severity_adjusted":"medium"}},{"finding":{"category":"god-file / control-plane concentration","confidence":"confirmed","evidence":"architecture.md: \"Tool Executor (companion/src/server.ts)\". Live file ends at line 5782. createToolExecutor mixes pack whitelist, tab leases, L2_GATE_TOOLS, critical-API forceConfirm, host_computer rate/mutex, MCP dispatch, and extension tool.execute. executeCompanionTool is a giant switch (spawn_worker…host_computer…shell). validateWsMessage, startServer, shutdown, pendingToolCalls, securityConfirmations all co-locate. message-router.ts is a second ~2343-line case switch (96 cases).","file":"companion/src/server.ts:494-560,790-820,2080-2184,2706-4025,4654-5041,5092-5781; docs/architecture.md:157-160","fix_hint":"Extract: connection/auth, tool-admission (L2 gates), companion-tool handlers, MCP execute, validateWsMessage protocol module, lifecycle. Keep createToolExecutor as thin router. Target <800 LOC per module; shared typed message map.","id":"XC-Architecture-1","impact":"Any gate edit has multi-domain blast radius; review/test isolation is weak (matches TEST-1 startServer replica). Cross-cutting regressions (originWs inconsistency SEC-1, abort incompleteness) cluster here because there is no session/tool-admission kernel with clear module boundaries.","prior_status":"partial","severity":"high","title":"server.ts owns auth, every L2 gate, companion tools, MCP, CU, and lifecycle (~5782 LOC)"},"verdict":{"evidence":"companion/src/server.ts L5781 setupGracefulShutdown; L494 export function createToolExecutor; L579-605 isToolAllowed/pack gate; L629-652 tab lease HARD; L687-721 COOKIE_TOOLS; L790-818 L2_GATE_TOOLS + forceConfirm path; L2105-2123 executeCompanionTool + originWs-bound securityConfirmations.request; L2705-4015 executeCompanionTool switch (spawn_worker…host_computer); L4025 executeMcpTool; L4654 validateWsMessage; L5092 startServer; L193/299 pendingToolCalls + securityConfirmations. docs/architecture.md L157-160: 'Tool Executor (companion/src/server.ts)'. Mitigations: imports from ./ws-auth, ./security-confirmation, ./security-policy, ./mcp, dynamic import ./orchestrator, ./board, ./packs; createToolExecutor exported and unit-tested without full startServer. message-router.ts: handleMessage ends ~L2342 with ~96 case arms (separate file, not all in server.ts).","finding_id":"XC-Architecture-1","real":true,"reason":"Confirmed: server.ts is a ~5782-LOC composition root; createToolExecutor mixes pack whitelist, tab leases, L2_GATE_TOOLS, confirmation, MCP/extension dispatch; executeCompanionTool is a large switch; architecture.md documents Tool Executor here; message-router is a second large case-switch. Severity is not high: domain logic is largely extracted (ws-auth, security-confirmation/policy, mcp/, orchestrator/, board/, host-use/, computer/, capability/), createToolExecutor is intentionally the single admission SoT (not 'no kernel'), and many tests exercise createToolExecutor without startServer. This is maintainability/blast-radius debt, not an unmitigated high-severity defect.","severity_adjusted":"medium"}},{"finding":{"category":"race/lifecycle","confidence":"confirmed","evidence":"Supersede only aborts controller then starts a new chatCreate on the same thread without awaiting the old run: `existing.abort(); abortControllers.delete(...);` then later `await chatCreate(...)`. Old run finally always does `abortControllers.delete(rest.thread_id); releaseMultiAgentLlmLoop(rest.thread_id)` — not generation-guarded, so it deletes the *new* controller and releases a multi-agent slot still held by the successor. On AbortError, adapter `deleteMessagesFrom(threadId, savedAssistantId)` slices from the old assistant inclusive, which also drops any user/tool messages the successor already appended after that id. Catch also sends `chat.aborted` for the thread while the new stream may still be live; extension applies SET_PROCESSING false + \"⏹ 已停止生成\" with only thread_id gate (no run id).","file":"companion/src/message-router.ts:433-517; companion/src/llm/adapter.ts:292,556-566,607-610,807,959-986; companion/src/threads/thread-manager.ts:561-575; chrome-extension/src/sidepanel/hooks/useWebSocket.ts:241-255","fix_hint":"Per-thread generation token (or AbortController identity): finally only deletes/releases if map entry === this run’s controller. Join supersede: await prior chatCreate settle (or rejectPendingForThread + wait tools) before new user message. Scope deleteMessagesFrom to messages owned by the aborted run (ids recorded this generation), not “everything after old assistant”. Stamp chat.aborted/done/error with run_id and ignore stale events in the extension.","id":"XC-Correctness-1","impact":"Resend/stop-by-resend during in-flight tools can: make the new turn un-abortable; free multi-agent LLM cap early (over-admit workers); delete the new user message and partial tape from disk; flash false stop UI while generation continues. Data