+| No new TCC copy | ✅ | None of the new strings ask users to approve node/host |
+
+### Blocking issues
+
+**1. `companion/tests/apps-add-flow.test.ts:166` — stale test, regressed by this diff**
+The test `non-.exe target → not_an_exe` injects `/opt/tools/run.bat` on non-Windows and expects rejection with code `not_an_exe`. The branch changed `add-flow.ts:237` to `if (isWin && !/\.exe$/i.test(expanded))` (Windows-only), so macOS `.bat` paths now skip the extension gate and fall through to `not_found` instead. Test was not updated.
+```
+✖ non-.exe target → not_an_exe (0.24875ms)
+  AssertionError: Missing expected rejection.
+```
+
+**2. `companion/tests/apps-config.test.ts:139` — stale test, regressed by this diff**
+The test `accepts a valid cli entry with empty-object cli_manifest placeholder` calls `validateAppEntry(cliEntry())` where `cliEntry()` sets `cli_manifest: {}`. The branch added strict `validateCliManifest` for kind=cli entries in types.ts:179-184, so `{}` is now rejected with `cli_manifest.schema_version must be 1`. Test was not updated.
+```
+✖ accepts a valid cli entry with empty-object cli_manifest placeholder (0.417ms)
+  actual:   'app "win.cli.ffmpeg" cli_manifest.schema_version must be 1'
+  expected: null
+```
+
+Both tests passed on the base commit (`007130b`); both fail on HEAD. They violate the master plan's stop gate F2-K (`npm --prefix companion test` green) and constitute "incomplete fixes / over-claiming" — the implementer changed behavior but did not update the two tests that verify the old behavior.
+
+### Non-blocking nits
+
+- `companion/src/apps/handlers.ts:364-367` — indentation drift (looks like mixed whitespace; the `if (entry.kind === "cli"...)` line and `const cap = maxPolicyForEntry(entry)` line are flush-left inside a case block). Functionally fine; cosmetic.
+- `companion/src/computer/model-handlers.ts:336` — user-visible error string `"实验层许可证已被拒绝，本层永久跳过（复位路径 = 手改 config.json…）"` is now stale: the same file (line 406-412) implements `reset_decline: true` to clear the flag from settings UI. The LICENSE_DECLINED message contradicts the new reset path.
+- `companion/src/computer/model-handlers.ts:437` — code comment `// 拒绝：永久跳过（复位 = 手改 config.json，不提供 UI 复位——裁决 2）` is similarly stale.
+- `companion/src/computer/qwen-vl-coords.ts` — `normalizeQwenVlPoint` is only referenced by its own test; not wired into any production click path (the actual normalization happens in `qwen-vl-worker.py`). Acts as algorithm mirror/documentation; not a bug.
+- No explicit test for the `apps.set_policy` L-CLI-1 cap (CLI → auto downgrade). The `apps.add` path is tested; the `set_policy` path is not.
+- ADR-020 capability declaration block (Surface/L2-classes/Compose/Autonomy/Trust/Channel) absent from the implementer prompt. The implementation correctly places things on the Surface axis and respects Pack-first / no-bare-middle-agent / trust-monotonicity, so this is a process nit, not a structural problem.
+
+### ADR-020 capability checklist
+
+- Axes fit: ✅ `host_cli` correctly on Surface (L2 host-side), not a "middle agent"
+- Pack-first: ✅ uses apps config + tool catalog, no new Pack surface
+- Confirm dialects: ✅ reuses existing SecurityPolicy L2 token (no new confirmation family)
+- Trust monotonicity: ✅ god-mode cannot skip host_cli (`capabilityForceConfirm` includes it)
+- originWs: token is bound to threadId via SecurityPolicy (consistent with host_computer precedent)
+- Experimental layers: Qwen3-VL still requires per-task re-L2 (PROMPT_ALWAYS_TAGS retains `computer.experimental_suggestion`)
+
+VERDICT: REJECT
